tc.research_name.ORDO_MATRIX=Ordo Usurpatory Matrix
tc.research_text.ORDO_MATRIX=You should rely more on automation, as a thaumaturge of the new age
tc.research_page.ORDO_MATRIX.1=Entering a new age, you grow tired of imitating the old masters' repetitive labour—verifying symmetry and waiting half a day for an infusion to finish. You cannot help shouting: "WTF!"<BR>....w? Wait—I have it!<BR>Now everything is different. Holding W led you to conceive this absurd yet utterly effortless, wheelchair-grade contraption. Then the rules should change: magic should not be this inconvenient!<BR>With it, you no longer need to arrange a pile of stabilizers; you can fast-forward the ritual at whatever speed you like.
tc.research_name.ARCANE_REPLICATOR=Arcane Aspect Replicator
tc.research_text.ARCANE_REPLICATOR=Echoes of the Aspects
tc.research_page.ARCANE_REPLICATOR.1=I have long wondered whether an aspect remembers its own shape after it is drawn out of matter.<BR>When I place a sample into this machine, it is not consumed. Instead, the machine acts as a mirror, projecting the aspect within the sample into the vessel beside it, again and again.<BR>As long as the sample remains, the projection continues; only when I switch off infinite mode does the sample return to my pack.<BR>It sounds like a perpetual motion machine, yet it creates nothing new — it merely copies the pattern of the same aspect into another place.<BR>At least, that is how I understand it for now.
tc.research_page.ARCANE_REPLICATOR.2=The operation is simple: place a sample on the left — an aspect shard or crystal essence will do; place the target on the right — a wand or crystal essence.<BR>Once infinite mode is enabled, the aspect is locked, the sample cannot be replaced, and the machine keeps infusing the target.<BR>The six faces can be toggled independently, and the rate decides how much is infused each tick.<BR>If you would rather not tune every machine by hand, copy its settings with an Arcane Ord-Record Shard and paste them onto another machine of the same kind.<BR>The recipe is as follows.
tc.research_name.ARCANE_EMANATOR=Arcane Essentia Emanator
tc.research_text.ARCANE_EMANATOR=An Essentia Spring That Never Runs Dry
tc.research_page.ARCANE_EMANATOR.1=Essentia is usually trapped in alembics, jars and tubes, like mist behind glass.<BR>I tried to keep it liquid inside the machine, and to write the state of "infinity" into its calculations.<BR>The result is somewhat absurd: it reports an essentia reserve that never decreases. Tubes may draw from it, yet it never runs empty.<BR>It has no suction and only gives; because it never demands, tubes can safely take from it.
tc.research_page.ARCANE_EMANATOR.2=Place a filled phial or crystal essence into the sample slot, lock the aspect, then enable infinite mode.<BR>With active output enabled, it pushes essentia toward adjacent tubes or devices at the chosen faces and rate; if jars are placed within its range, every jar in range is topped up each tick.<BR>The range box can be kept visible so you can confirm which jars are covered.<BR>It stores no essentia; it merely makes essentia appear where it is needed. Do keep that in mind.<BR>The recipe is as follows.
tc.research_name.ARCANE_SHARD=Arcane Ord-Record Shard
tc.research_text.ARCANE_SHARD=A Machine's Choices, Written Down
tc.research_page.ARCANE_SHARD.1=Every time I finish tuning one arcane machine, I have to repeat the same motions on the next one.<BR>That tried my patience. So I bound a small quartz shard to a scrying lens and tried to make it "remember" a machine's settings when right-clicked.<BR>It did. Not the position of the block, but the invisible order inside it — which faces are open, what the rate is, which aspect is locked.<BR>I call it the Ord-Record Shard.
tc.research_page.ARCANE_SHARD.2=Sneak-use the shard to copy an arcane machine's settings; use it on another machine of the same kind to paste them.<BR>It only accepts its own family: the Aspect Replicator, the Essentia Emanator and the Ordo Usurpatory Matrix. Any other machine only earns a warning.<BR>The shard stores no samples, essentia or altar coordinates — only settings — so it is safe to copy around.<BR>The recipe is as follows.
tooltip.infwhat.ordo_usurpatory_matrix.normal=You should rely more on automation, as a thaumaturge of the new age
tooltip.infwhat.ordo_usurpatory_matrix.shift.1=▸ The altar's native calculation path? Intercept it. The result? Redirect it. A Broken Thing ought to be broken
tooltip.infwhat.ordo_usurpatory_matrix.lore=Stabilizers? Piss off. Ritual? Fast-forward. If the rules are in the way, rewrite them until they aren't.
